This is the shared-index hazard CLAUDE.md warns about, arriving from the
direction we do not usually guard: not `git commit -a` sweeping a peer's work,
but a path-scoped commit of one file that a peer also had in flight. Path
scoping bounds which files you take, not which edits inside them. For a file
several agents have reason to touch, say so before editing it — the way debt.yml
was claimed in this same session.
